1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,140
Section one.

2
00:00:02,902 --> 00:00:04,442
The problem and the product.

3
00:00:05,584 --> 00:00:07,644
GitHub Manager helps you discover,

4
00:00:08,784 --> 00:00:10,624
understand, and organize repositories.

5
00:00:11,865 --> 00:00:14,825
The purpose is to turn a scattered collection into

6
00:00:14,825 --> 00:00:18,806
a workspace whose relationships you can inspect and change.

7
00:00:28,807 --> 00:00:30,367
Imagine starting an API project.

8
00:00:31,759 --> 00:00:32,959
You have your own services,

9
00:00:33,719 --> 00:00:36,619
shared repositories, and libraries starred for later.

10
00:00:38,511 --> 00:00:40,511
Names and programming languages help you search.

11
00:00:41,424 --> 00:00:44,464
They do not explain which pieces support the same

12
00:00:44,464 --> 00:00:44,924
initiative.

13
00:00:46,756 --> 00:00:50,456
Two Python repositories may serve entirely different purposes.

14
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:58,620
GitHub remains the source of repository facts:

15
00:00:59,660 --> 00:00:59,780
identity,

16
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:00,580
links,

17
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:03,100
visibility, and available metadata.

18
00:01:04,369 --> 00:01:07,009
The application builds selected evidence locally.

19
00:01:08,157 --> 00:01:11,637
AI proposes an organization, and the user reviews it.

20
00:01:12,466 --> 00:01:16,825
This separation matters because a convenient suggestion must not

21
00:01:16,825 --> 00:01:19,726
quietly replace a fact or a deliberate decision.

22
00:01:24,887 --> 00:01:28,867
We will follow Orion, an authored synthetic patient-intake

23
00:01:28,867 --> 00:01:29,467
application.

24
00:01:31,097 --> 00:01:35,457
Its displayed classification comes from a saved real API

25
00:01:35,457 --> 00:01:35,977
test.

26
00:01:37,287 --> 00:01:40,807
We will also use a public FastAPI library as

27
00:01:40,807 --> 00:01:41,467
a contrast.

28
00:01:42,877 --> 00:01:46,537
These examples explain the mechanics; they are not a

29
00:01:46,537 --> 00:01:48,877
new account recording or a new benchmark.

30
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:55,420
Section two.

31
00:01:56,633 --> 00:01:57,773
Organization vocabulary.

32
00:01:59,167 --> 00:02:02,487
Before classification, we need to define what a relationship

33
00:02:02,487 --> 00:02:03,007
means.

34
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:07,060
The purpose is to keep an initiative, a capability,

35
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:11,360
and a technology from becoming one confusing pile of

36
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:11,480
labels.

37
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:24,540
A Project answers which product or initiative a repository

38
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:25,040
supports.

39
00:02:25,868 --> 00:02:29,288
A Domain groups those Projects into a broader area.

40
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:33,996
A Topic describes a primary capability or subject.

41
00:02:35,124 --> 00:02:38,844
A Tag describes technology or another useful characteristic.

42
00:02:40,312 --> 00:02:43,112
For Orion, the examples are the clinical platform,

43
00:02:43,832 --> 00:02:46,092
Healthcare, Web APIs, and Python.

44
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:54,110
A repository may support more than one Project.

45
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:58,440
Its Domains derive through those Project memberships;

46
00:02:59,140 --> 00:03:01,740
the classifier does not assign Domains independently.

47
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:06,850
Topics and Tags remain useful when no Project applies.

48
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:11,560
The application's Topics are separate from the native topics

49
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,500
supplied by GitHub.

50
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:21,530
The Orion application uses FastAPI and Python.

51
00:03:23,209 --> 00:03:26,509
The FastAPI library is itself a reusable framework.

52
00:03:28,707 --> 00:03:30,827
Sharing those words does not make the library part

53
00:03:30,827 --> 00:03:31,367
of Orion.

54
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:36,246
Under the primary-label policy, incidental capabilities are

55
00:03:36,246 --> 00:03:39,906
omitted, and a library's own name is not automatically

56
00:03:39,906 --> 00:03:41,146
its dependency Tag.

57
00:03:42,645 --> 00:03:46,425
Next, we decide what evidence can support that distinction.

58
00:03:51,997 --> 00:03:52,797
Section three.

59
00:03:54,495 --> 00:03:55,175
Context engineering.

60
00:03:56,534 --> 00:03:59,394
Its purpose is to choose what information the model

61
00:03:59,394 --> 00:03:59,834
sees,

62
00:04:00,574 --> 00:04:04,014
what that information means, and which boundaries remain outside

63
00:04:04,014 --> 00:04:04,494
the model.

64
00:04:06,232 --> 00:04:09,512
A longer prompt is not automatically a better decision.

65
00:04:18,533 --> 00:04:21,393
We separate trusted source facts,

66
00:04:22,793 --> 00:04:26,233
untrusted repository prose, user-owned organization,

67
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,453
and execution identity.

68
00:04:29,793 --> 00:04:30,653
Canonical IDs,

69
00:04:31,633 --> 00:04:31,953
rejections,

70
00:04:32,753 --> 00:04:35,693
revisions, and evidence hashes constrain the operation.

71
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:39,733
The application does not send every stored record to

72
00:04:39,733 --> 00:04:40,173
the model.

73
00:04:41,153 --> 00:04:41,873
For example,

74
00:04:42,533 --> 00:04:46,313
protected decisions filter candidates before prompting rather than

75
00:04:46,313 --> 00:04:48,793
becoming an entire conversation history.

76
00:04:54,150 --> 00:04:58,010
Hosted input is restricted to verified public repositories and

77
00:04:58,010 --> 00:05:00,070
synthetic fixtures in this implementation.

78
00:05:02,555 --> 00:05:06,195
Private or unknown visibility fails closed, including phrases

79
00:05:06,195 --> 00:05:07,615
derived from private text.

80
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,840
Local rules can still help organization.

81
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:15,126
Narrow cleaning patterns are hygiene,

82
00:05:15,786 --> 00:05:19,026
not a complete secret scanner or prompt-injection defense.

83
00:05:20,871 --> 00:05:22,891
The model has no tools with which to act

84
00:05:22,891 --> 00:05:24,071
on README instructions.

85
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,800
The working runtime is local Next.js,

86
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,680
FastAPI, and SQLite.

87
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:39,200
LangChain connects structured requests; it does not own the

88
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:40,160
application's memory.

89
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:44,680
During development, user decisions outrank approved design,

90
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,740
plans, and historical discussion.

91
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,280
Phase zero checked access;

92
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,160
phase zero point five checked AI readiness;

93
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:55,600
phase zero point nine delivered the local app.

94
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,620
Cloud runtime remains deferred.

95
00:06:03,787 --> 00:06:04,667
Section four.

96
00:06:06,277 --> 00:06:07,237
Evidence and chunking.

97
00:06:08,767 --> 00:06:11,127
The purpose is to preserve the sentence that explains

98
00:06:11,127 --> 00:06:14,767
a repository, while excluding material that is unlikely to

99
00:06:14,767 --> 00:06:15,567
help organization.

100
00:06:16,897 --> 00:06:20,717
We begin with a README, not an AI-generated summary.

101
00:06:29,837 --> 00:06:34,617
The extractor parses Markdown blocks and applies heading-based

102
00:06:34,617 --> 00:06:35,137
selection.

103
00:06:36,257 --> 00:06:38,257
Metadata becomes evidence zero;

104
00:06:39,457 --> 00:06:42,057
selected README text receives additional IDs.

105
00:06:43,257 --> 00:06:47,777
For Orion, evidence one says: patient intake API

106
00:06:47,777 --> 00:06:50,137
for the Orion Clinical Platform.

107
00:06:50,917 --> 00:06:53,457
Uses FastAPI and Python.

108
00:06:54,257 --> 00:06:56,277
The language metadata is empty,

109
00:06:56,917 --> 00:07:00,157
so Python is supported by prose rather than an

110
00:07:00,157 --> 00:07:01,577
invented GitHub value.

111
00:07:06,847 --> 00:07:09,447
The input byte ceiling limits the fetched document.

112
00:07:10,902 --> 00:07:13,942
Selected blocks and total evidence have character bounds.

113
00:07:15,217 --> 00:07:19,817
The compact classification profile then keeps metadata, up to

114
00:07:19,817 --> 00:07:22,757
two README records, and up to eight phrase strings.

115
00:07:24,312 --> 00:07:26,412
Exact request tokens are counted later.

116
00:07:27,467 --> 00:07:31,047
Hashes bind the selected content and configuration.

117
00:07:32,642 --> 00:07:36,482
Offsets identify cleaned text, not original README line numbers.

118
00:07:42,063 --> 00:07:45,603
Heading rules are inspectable and avoid a hosted summarization

119
00:07:45,603 --> 00:07:49,543
pass, but can cut sentences or crowd out better

120
00:07:49,543 --> 00:07:49,963
evidence.

121
00:07:51,789 --> 00:07:56,149
Format noise, late negation, and multilingual headings need tests.

122
00:07:57,294 --> 00:08:00,334
The app received a separately versioned cleanup wrapper;

123
00:08:01,354 --> 00:08:03,854
frozen benchmark profiles stayed unchanged.

124
00:08:06,060 --> 00:08:09,540
Retrieval can see full selected evidence that compact generation

125
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:09,920
omits,

126
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,740
so both stages need their own checks.

127
00:08:18,130 --> 00:08:18,950
Section five.

128
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:20,620
Local algorithms.

129
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:25,190
Their purpose is to expose compact signals before an

130
00:08:25,190 --> 00:08:26,030
expensive decision.

131
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:31,000
We use phrase extraction and corpus counts, but those

132
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,620
numbers do not establish initiative membership or semantic

133
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:35,260
understanding.

134
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,860
RAKE splits around stopwords and punctuation.

135
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:52,280
Word frequency and co-occurrence contribute to phrase scores.

136
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:55,680
Our configuration considers one to four words,

137
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:57,720
retains up to twenty candidates,

138
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:01,340
normalizes duplicates, and checks source spans.

139
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:02,700
In Orion,

140
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:07,200
patient intake API and Orion clinical platform each score

141
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:07,660
nine.

142
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:10,980
FastAPI and Python score one.

143
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,720
Those are weights, not probabilities.

144
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:23,040
YAKE was compared offline using local document features such

145
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:23,800
as position,

146
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,060
capitalization, and frequency.

147
00:09:27,155 --> 00:09:29,515
It is not the production extractor.

148
00:09:30,730 --> 00:09:34,910
Its measured runtime included repeated process startup, so the

149
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:37,190
ratio is not an intrinsic speed comparison.

150
00:09:39,365 --> 00:09:42,365
Corpus document frequency counts a term once per repository.

151
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:47,900
That pretest table is different from the concept-document IDF

152
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:49,160
used in retrieval.

153
00:09:50,895 --> 00:09:54,435
The installed YAKE artifact's licensing also remained an adoption

154
00:09:54,435 --> 00:09:54,915
concern.

155
00:10:00,297 --> 00:10:02,577
A bag of phrases loses relationships,

156
00:10:03,317 --> 00:10:04,457
including the word not.

157
00:10:05,843 --> 00:10:07,263
Purpose prose must survive.

158
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:11,030
In one historical FastAPI ablation,

159
00:10:11,910 --> 00:10:15,530
adding RAKE phrases used more input tokens without changing

160
00:10:15,530 --> 00:10:17,310
the unwanted secondary labels.

161
00:10:18,176 --> 00:10:21,756
That single case proves neither that phrases always help

162
00:10:22,296 --> 00:10:23,676
nor that they are unnecessary.

163
00:10:25,963 --> 00:10:29,423
The product also has no learned project-clustering engine or

164
00:10:29,423 --> 00:10:31,023
automatically learned rules.

165
00:10:36,513 --> 00:10:37,547
Section six.

166
00:10:37,547 --> 00:10:39,147
Taxonomy intelligence.

167
00:10:40,321 --> 00:10:43,161
The purpose is to propose a vocabulary for a

168
00:10:43,161 --> 00:10:43,281
collection.

169
00:10:44,515 --> 00:10:47,395
This is different from assigning labels to one repository.

170
00:10:48,989 --> 00:10:50,889
Discovery can suggest new concepts;

171
00:10:51,789 --> 00:10:54,469
classification must use concepts already approved.

172
00:11:03,210 --> 00:11:07,670
The saved discovery request contained thirty compact profiles:

173
00:11:08,770 --> 00:11:09,630
ten public samples

174
00:11:10,290 --> 00:11:11,830
and twenty authored fixtures.

175
00:11:13,210 --> 00:11:13,990
Orion's API,

176
00:11:14,710 --> 00:11:15,070
UI,

177
00:11:15,810 --> 00:11:19,310
booking, and audit records supplied related purpose evidence.

178
00:11:20,250 --> 00:11:24,210
The model proposed Orion Clinical Platform with a Clinical

179
00:11:24,210 --> 00:11:27,730
Operations parent and supporting repository IDs.

180
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:31,910
Its twenty proposals were a draft, not a published

181
00:11:31,910 --> 00:11:32,610
organization.

182
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:41,700
The app samples owner and language buckets using a

183
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,580
deterministic round-robin approach.

184
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:49,550
Collection packing uses a conservative byte allowance before exact

185
00:11:49,550 --> 00:11:50,290
token counting,

186
00:11:51,310 --> 00:11:53,690
shortening records and pruning phrases where necessary.

187
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:57,700
This can miss structure outside the cohort.

188
00:11:59,570 --> 00:12:03,190
The saved direct collection request used its original packing

189
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:06,510
path, so its token counts cannot be attributed to

190
00:12:06,510 --> 00:12:07,670
a later optimization.

191
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,820
Publication normalizes names and aliases,

192
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:19,520
including Unicode handling, and checks reservations.

193
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:23,160
A visible name can conflict with an alias or

194
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,260
archived concept.

195
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:29,020
The app exposes the conflicting record and offers opt-in

196
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:29,560
reuse,

197
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:30,520
renaming,

198
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:32,180
removal, or exclusion.

199
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:36,360
These deterministic checks protect canonical consistency.

200
00:12:36,910 --> 00:12:41,020
Similar language is not permission for an automatic semantic

201
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:41,440
merge.

202
00:12:47,523 --> 00:12:48,083
Section seven.

203
00:12:48,763 --> 00:12:49,683
Retrieval.

204
00:12:50,183 --> 00:12:53,343
Its purpose is to find plausible concepts from the

205
00:12:53,343 --> 00:12:54,423
approved vocabulary.

206
00:12:55,703 --> 00:12:59,603
The repository evidence is the query; concept names,

207
00:13:00,483 --> 00:13:03,183
definitions, and aliases are the searchable documents.

208
00:13:04,063 --> 00:13:06,063
A shortlist is not a decision.

209
00:13:15,757 --> 00:13:19,517
The method called TF-IDF in the code is actually

210
00:13:19,517 --> 00:13:20,957
binary-IDF cosine.

211
00:13:22,311 --> 00:13:26,431
It weights less common registry terms and normalizes overlap,

212
00:13:27,211 --> 00:13:29,571
while repeated terms do not increase frequency.

213
00:13:30,925 --> 00:13:34,465
A name or alias whose tokens all appear adds

214
00:13:34,465 --> 00:13:36,425
three once.

215
00:13:36,939 --> 00:13:39,459
Token order and positive assertion are not required.

216
00:13:41,253 --> 00:13:44,733
Positive candidates are ranked by kind, with stable-ID ties

217
00:13:44,733 --> 00:13:46,153
and bounded limits.

218
00:13:51,983 --> 00:13:54,943
Orion retrieves its own Project, Web APIs,

219
00:13:55,723 --> 00:13:57,303
FastAPI, and Python.

220
00:13:58,743 --> 00:14:01,883
Forge also surfaces through platform, and Package Management

221
00:14:01,883 --> 00:14:02,703
through Python.

222
00:14:03,503 --> 00:14:06,543
The strong Orion score includes the alias boost.

223
00:14:07,583 --> 00:14:08,903
These are ranking scores,

224
00:14:09,723 --> 00:14:11,103
not membership probabilities.

225
00:14:12,463 --> 00:14:15,823
The next stage must distinguish actual purpose evidence from

226
00:14:15,823 --> 00:14:17,223
distracting shared words.

227
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:26,480
BM25 was compared offline with the same alias boost

228
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,560
and candidate caps.

229
00:14:29,148 --> 00:14:32,608
It adds saturated term frequency and document-length

230
00:14:32,608 --> 00:14:33,348
normalization.

231
00:14:35,216 --> 00:14:36,576
On the small reused comparison,

232
00:14:37,256 --> 00:14:40,196
both lexical methods covered the expected evaluation labels;

233
00:14:41,036 --> 00:14:42,476
alias-only missed four Topics.

234
00:14:43,625 --> 00:14:45,205
That supports feasibility,

235
00:14:45,924 --> 00:14:48,065
not sparse superiority over dense search.

236
00:14:49,933 --> 00:14:53,673
There is no embedding query, neural reranker, or autonomous

237
00:14:53,673 --> 00:14:55,573
retrieval agent in the current product.

238
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:01,220
Section eight.

239
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:02,140
Augmentation.

240
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:06,520
The purpose is to assemble a decision-ready request from

241
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:09,140
the evidence and retrieved possibilities.

242
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,740
Retrieval supplies options.

243
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:16,100
Augmentation explains those options and the rules for selecting

244
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:16,540
them.

245
00:15:25,427 --> 00:15:29,107
For Orion, the payload includes repository identity,

246
00:15:30,007 --> 00:15:31,467
public or synthetic source status,

247
00:15:32,187 --> 00:15:32,407
revision,

248
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:33,687
evidence hash,

249
00:15:34,507 --> 00:15:37,567
selected evidence, phrase strings, and candidate records.

250
00:15:38,967 --> 00:15:41,787
Evidence one preserves the patient-intake sentence.

251
00:15:42,687 --> 00:15:46,807
Candidate records contain canonical ID, kind, name, and

252
00:15:46,807 --> 00:15:47,187
description.

253
00:15:48,267 --> 00:15:51,547
Aliases helped retrieval but are not serialized into those

254
00:15:51,547 --> 00:15:52,387
candidate objects.

255
00:15:53,467 --> 00:15:55,927
Expected evaluation labels are never supplied.

256
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:03,893
The system instructions require supported approved IDs,

257
00:16:04,873 --> 00:16:05,773
primary-purpose Topics,

258
00:16:06,393 --> 00:16:08,113
and primary implementation Tags.

259
00:16:09,101 --> 00:16:12,201
Shared frameworks do not prove initiative membership.

260
00:16:13,748 --> 00:16:14,568
Negation matters;

261
00:16:15,708 --> 00:16:16,788
multiple Projects are allowed.

262
00:16:17,955 --> 00:16:20,975
Unsupported input can produce no match or a request

263
00:16:20,975 --> 00:16:22,055
for more context.

264
00:16:23,643 --> 00:16:27,323
User decisions remain application constraints rather than an

265
00:16:27,323 --> 00:16:29,343
invitation for the model to overrule them.

266
00:16:34,227 --> 00:16:37,047
A strict response schema describes assignments,

267
00:16:37,867 --> 00:16:38,387
evidence references,

268
00:16:39,147 --> 00:16:39,447
reasons,

269
00:16:40,067 --> 00:16:41,226
status, and summary.

270
00:16:41,226 --> 00:16:44,746
LangChain binds that schema to the hosted request.

271
00:16:46,165 --> 00:16:49,565
The harness inspects the assembled messages and schema before

272
00:16:49,565 --> 00:16:50,745
counting input tokens.

273
00:16:51,964 --> 00:16:55,784
This is retrieval-augmented structured classification, with

274
00:16:55,784 --> 00:16:57,244
durable application memory.

275
00:16:58,103 --> 00:17:02,623
It is not a conversational document-question-answering agent, and

276
00:17:02,623 --> 00:17:05,503
adaptive budgets do not turn it into Adaptive RAG.

277
00:17:10,733 --> 00:17:11,753
Section nine.

278
